  "id": "DrugBank_DB00885 - MONDO_4784",
  "verbalization": "Pemirolast is associated with Allergic Asthma through a series of mechanistically linked pathways. The drug is indicated for Asthma, which is further linked to Allergic Asthma via Reproterol and Ibudilast, both of which are known to modulate inflammatory responses. This suggests that Pemirolast may exert a therapeutic effect on Allergic Asthma through a pathway involving inflammatory mediators. Additionally, Pemirolast is also linked to Intrinsic Asthma, which is further linked to Zileuton, a phosphodiesterase-4 inhibitor, and then to Allergic Asthma. These connections imply that Pemirolast may act through a shared mechanism in the treatment of allergic asthma, possibly by modulating inflammatory pathways or immune responses. The evidence supports a potential role for Pemirolast in the management of Allergic Asthma, though further mechanistic validation is required to confirm its direct therapeutic effect.",
